# Installed scanner and local rules only. Sequential source analysis.
name: Native rule gaps retain findings for explicit partial review and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/native_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/alpha-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT READY | imported-map
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Scan | accepted-map
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/native-scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | native-prerequisite
expect: recommended reuse
ask: Does the prerequisite card disclose local indexing and let the operator explicitly reuse the cached context before starting this scoped scanner?
keys: r
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/native_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART unselected
submit: workbench
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT partial | partial-120x36
expect: partial
expect: Incomplete coverage
expect: incompatible-fixture-rule
ask: Does Scan retain its finding and explain the actual omitted rule before asking the operator to acknowledge incomplete coverage?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 incompatible-fixture-rule | partial-160x48
ask: At 160x48, is the scoped engine gap readable with one retained finding and no complete-coverage claim?
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 incompatible-fixture-rule | partial-96x89
ask: At 96x89, does the full partial result remain readable without accepting or starting work?
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept partial | partial-80x24
ask: At 80x24, are partial status and the controls for reading and acknowledging the result understandable?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept partial | partial-60x20
ask: At 60x20, can the operator distinguish retained evidence from incomplete coverage and reach its details?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept | partial-40x12
ask: At 40x12, is incomplete work identifiable and can the operator read the rest before accepting it?
nav-mode:
keys: NPage NPage
require-live-snap: 15 7-10/10 | partial-40x12-paged
ask: Can the operator read the concrete native coverage gap at 40x12 using the same visible controls?
resize: 120x36
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | acknowledged-native
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/native_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART selected
expect: 1 remaining
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/open-finding.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 needs_review | retained-observation
submit: dismiss false_positive Labeled local rule fixture
require-live-snap: 25 rejected_false_positive | reviewed-observation
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 1 findings · 1 reviewed | native-report
ask: Can the operator report the retained observation after an explicit human decision while incomplete Scan remains durable?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scan
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 25 Incomplete coverage | restarted-scan
expect: partial acknowledged
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/native_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After restart without color, do the selected partial run, concrete gap and retained decision remain readable without another scan?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
